From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:16:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/30] drama: the temporal codebook tower

The tower turns a backbone row into a frame's ten codebook values: four shared and nine residual layers whose
cache keeps every preceding text and audio row, a semantic head and the reference sampler (temperature, top-p over
the whole vocabulary, then top-k). Its projections run on cuBLASLt; drama_tower.cu holds the mixer, norms, RoPE,
attention and sampling kernels.
